Changed: A DoFHandler on a parallel::shared::Triangulation with artificial
cells now enumerates degrees of freedom in the same way as on a
parallel::distributed::Triangulation: only locally owned and ghost cells
carry degree of freedom indices, artificial cells do not. Previously, all
cells carried valid indices. As a consequence, the numbering of degrees of
freedom within the locally owned ranges changes. The following functions
are no longer available for such triangulations, because they need the
degrees of freedom on all cells: DoFTools::get_subdomain_association(),
DoFTools::count_dofs_with_subdomain_association(),
DoFTools::locally_owned_dofs_per_subdomain(),
DoFTools::locally_relevant_dofs_per_subdomain(),
DoFRenumbering::subdomain_wise(), and Legacy::SolutionTransfer. Use
Utilities::MPI::all_gather() on DoFHandler::locally_owned_dofs() and
SolutionTransfer instead. Without artificial cells, nothing changes.
<br>
(Matthias Maier, 2026/11/27)
